> associator 100.1+i, 100.2+j, 100.3+k
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 503005003/500 + 253754i/25 + 993983j/100 + 253258k/25 - (503005003/500 + 253754i/25 + 993983j/100 + 253258k/25) = 1.164153218e-10
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator 1000.1+e1, 1000.2+e2, 1000.3+e3
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 166099618095/166 + 25037504 e1/25 + 99939983 e2/100 + 25032508 e3/25 - (166099618095/166 + 25037504 e1/25 + 99939983 e2/100 + 25032508 e3/25) = -1.192092896e-07
  the product of these three is associative (in the octonions)
> associator (1+i)/3, (1+j)/7, (1+k)/11
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 2i/231 + 2k/231 - (2i/231 + 2k/231) = 0i + 0k
  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)
> associator e1, e2, e4
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
> associator e1/1000, e2/1000, e4/1000
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 1e-09 e7 - (-1e-09 e7) = 2e-09 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
> associator 1000000000+e1, 1000000000+e2, 1000000000+e4
[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = 1e+27 + 1e+18 e1 + 1e+18 e2 + 1e+18 e4 - (1e+27 + 1e+18 e1 + 1e+18 e2 + 1e+18 e4) = 2 e7
  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)
